/// How the coordinator fuses the per-shard leg results of a hybrid query.
public nonisolated enum Ai_Protomolt_Search_V1_FusionMode: SwiftProtobuf.Enum, Swift.CaseIterable {
  public typealias RawValue = Int

  /// Unused zero value; resolves to FUSION_MODE_CASCADE.
  case unspecified // = 0

  /// Shards return RAW per-leg lists (ShardLegs); the coordinator
  /// merges each leg across shards by raw score into GLOBAL rankings and
  /// applies single-level RRF over them. With globally comparable scores
  /// per leg (shared calibration for vectors, global stats for BM25) this
  /// is EXACTLY the monolithic result for k <= leg_k: any doc in the true
  /// global top-leg_k of a leg is in its shard's local top-leg_k (local
  /// rank <= global rank), so the union of shard lists contains the exact
  /// global top-leg_k and merging by score reconstructs it.
  case globalRank // = 1

  /// Fallback for incomparable scores: each shard RRF-fuses its legs
  /// locally (HybridShard) and the coordinator RRF-merges the shard lists.
  /// Rank-based and therefore scale-free, but NOT partition-independent —
  /// shard-local ranks are compressed relative to global ranks, so the
  /// result can differ from a monolithic index.
  case twoLevel // = 2

  /// What an unset fusion_mode resolves to. Cascade, no score fusion:
  /// phase 1 generates vector candidates through the floor-sharing bidi
  /// path (cross-shard early termination applies — the cutoff IS the
  /// savings, no leg_k hits per shard), with a TIE-COMPLETE cutoff:
  /// the candidate pool is
  /// {score >= s_k} where s_k is the global k-th vector score, so the
  /// pool can exceed k by the boundary tie-group size. Phase 2 reranks
  /// the pool by BM25 (global stats, candidate-scoped scoring per owning
  /// shard) and returns the top k. Vector recall is a GATE here:
  /// keyword-strong but vector-weak docs are not surfaced — use
  /// Bm25Search for pure lexical queries, or GLOBAL_RANK for true fusion.
  case cascade // = 3

  /// Score-based fusion (the normalize + weighted-combine family):
  /// shards return RAW per-leg lists exactly as in GLOBAL_RANK; the
  /// coordinator merges each leg into one global list, truncates it
  /// TIE-COMPLETE to leg_k (the retained set is {score >= s_k} with s_k
  /// the leg's leg_k-th best — score-defined, hence layout-invariant),
  /// normalizes the retained scores per leg (ScoreNormalization) and
  /// combines each doc's normalized leg scores (ScoreCombination)
  /// weighted by vector_weight/bm25_weight. Rank-free: score GAPS
  /// survive fusion — a runaway leg leader stays far ahead where RRF
  /// compresses every gap to the fixed distance between adjacent ranks.
  /// Requires globally comparable scores per leg, same as GLOBAL_RANK.
  case scoreBlend // = 4

